# PROBE disjoint-union. A is the disjoint union of B and C, so D ⊑ B ⊓ C is unsatisfiable, and B ⊑ A.
# construct: DisjointUnion
# expect: unsat :D
# expect: sub :B :A
# expect-not: unsat :B

@prefix :     <http://example.org/t#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

<http://example.org/t> a owl:Ontology .
:A a owl:Class . :B a owl:Class . :C a owl:Class . :D a owl:Class .
:D rdfs:subClassOf :B .
:D rdfs:subClassOf :C .
:A owl:disjointUnionOf ( :B :C ) .
